// # BOARD HONESTY CHECK — 2026-08-19
//
// Logline: Spot-check every [x] (done) claim in the 9 process boards against on-disk reality.
//
// Setup: Date 2026-08-19. Cwd /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA. 9 boards read. For each [x] row, resolve the cited lock file, check it exists, and (where feasible) read the file to test the claim. Mark [x] true, [?] unverifiable, or [ ] failed.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Find every [x] row across the 9 boards.
//   2. Resolve the cited lock file:line on disk.
//   3. Read file content to test the claim where small.
//   4. Emit a per-board table with verdict and evidence.
//   5. Summarize totals and name the failed claims.

## 1. Method

  - Read all 9 boards: START.oot, RULES.oot, NORTHSTAR.oot, MOONSHOTS.oot, ROADMAP.oot, SHIPPED.oot, FORMAT.oot, SECURITY.oot, WORKFLOW.oot.
  - Grep for `^\s*\[x\]` in every board. Result: 0 in 8 boards, 70 in ROADMAP.oot only.
  - The other 8 boards use prose (`done`, `proved`, `real`, `verified`). The task targets [x] markers, so the other 8 boards have no [x] rows to verify.
  - For each ROADMAP.oot [x] row, find the cited lock file. The convention is bare filename. Locks live in ooda/scripts/, ooda/fixtures/, or ooda/std/prove/.
  - File-exists check: `ls -la` on each cited path. Verdict Y / N.
  - Content check: read the lock file header (4-element Academy) and the failing-condition strings. Verdict Y (matches claim), ? (exists, content not spot-checked), or N (contradicted).
  - Spot-checked in full: ~12 lock files + cli/main.oo + openOODA.github.io/install + bootstrap/seed/oodac + registry + wiki/ docs/ removal.
  - Did not run any smoke. Did not edit any board. No shell mutation beyond read.

