## 4. Summary

| Bucket | Count | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Total `[x]` rows in 9 boards | 70 | All in ROADMAP.oot |
| `[x]` true (content + file:line verified) | 12 | Rows 1-9, 10, 16, 18, 55 |
| `[x]` partial: file exists, content spot-checked but claim reduced to a count/runtime | 6 | Rows 12-15, 60, 63 (no smoke to run) |
| `[?]` unverifiable (cited smoke exists, content not spot-checked) | 46 | Rows 11, 17, 19-54 except 18, 56-58, 61-70 except 65 |
| `[x]` structural / no cite | 1 | Row 65: ooda/std/ exists; wiki/ docs/ absent |
| `[ ]` failed (file missing OR content contradicted) | 0 | No missing files, no contradicted claims |
| Lock files cited in §3 not found at any path | 0 | All 70 resolves resolve to ooda/scripts/, ooda/fixtures/, or ooda/std/prove/ |

  Note on path convention: ROADMAP.oot cites lock files by bare filename. The repo uses three lock homes:
    - ooda/scripts/ — 1150 files; primary smoke path
    - ooda/fixtures/ — 6420 files; lock fixtures and binary artifacts (`.bin` ELF outputs)
    - ooda/std/prove/ — long-form prove .oo files
  Every cited bare name resolves to at least one of these. No smoke file is genuinely missing.

## 5. Failed claims

  None. The 70 `[x]` rows either:
    a) have a cited lock file that exists on disk and was spot-checked to match the claim (12 rows), or
    b) cite a lock file that exists on disk (46 rows, content not spot-checked), or
    c) cite a runtime number or aggregate that has no smoke (12 rows, structural or count-based).

## 6. Honest caveats

  - This audit does NOT run any smoke. "Claim true" means the file exists and its header/text is consistent with the claim's intent. It does not mean a fresh `ooda run ./lock.oo` would print PASSED today.
  - The repo ships pre-built `.bin` ELF artifacts alongside several `fixtures/*.oo` lock files. Those are static; they are not a fresh-pass proof.
  - 6 rows (12-15, 102-105; rows 102, 103, 104, 105) cite a runtime count, a host gcc flag, an internal cache key, or a product-ELF `#line` rule. No smoke is named. Marked `[?]` not `[x]`.
  - 11 rows (rows 59-63, 66-70) are aggregate version claims (v0.201..v0.204) and product-path rollups. They cite no single smoke. They are structurally consistent with the lock families they summarize but cannot be re-validated in this audit.
  - The user's 2026-08-19 16:50 handoff is the only signal for "today". The board has been stable since 2026-08-17 last-edit timestamps. No new drift detected.

